[Music]  working at the council is indeed quite  special because it is a new institution  but really it is the place where  European politics is shaped every day  it's the place where the action is it's  the place where you leaders meet where  world leaders come to visit all the time  we have a lot of press and media  attention and a lot of journalists in  this building so I think also for  trainees it's a really great experience  to see how Europe works at the highest  political level one of the main things  that I really liked about the  traineeship was the fact that we were we  were not that many trainees compared to  the other institutions in the other  institution there are hundreds of  trainees but here at the council we were  only 60 or so so we really became like a  tight-knit group we kind of like made a  little family for ourselves here and  then really got to know each other and  you know build this network and I think  that was one of the main take outs and  also what Alexandra said about being at  the heart of European politics also one  of the amazing things all European  citizens can apply who have at least a  bachelor degree the main aim of or  traineeship is just that both trainees  and or institution benefits from it so  trainees got a meaningful work and they  get a deeper understanding of the work  of the council and the EU and the  council benefit from the fresh input  from the trainees  [Music]  there's no age limit although I have to  say the most of - or trainees are young  graduates what we are we also welcome  other people who are changing their  careers or they're purchasing lifelong  learning so they are also very welcome  to apply as well the eligibility  criteria is that you need to have  finished your first cycle of studies  that means three years of university  studies which results in a bachelor  degree and you should have earned a  bachelor degree before applying but it's  okay if you don't have the degree in  your hand until you sign the traineeship  agreement we also have another  traineeship program which we call  compulsory traineeship as part of your  studies the conditions are different the  main difference is that you don't need  to have a degree in order to apply but  all the conditions and the criteria is  explained on your website you can apply  and you can get in as a trainee  even with solely the knowledge of  English but then we also had a lot of  friends in the traineeship group who  were mainly speaking French during their  work hours and during their time as a  trainee so it really depends and a lot  of people knew both languages so it's  really a mixture of like English  speakers mainly French speakers and then  you know both and it's very common to  people have several languages that they  speak the more languages you speak the  more first style you are so you don't  have to have French for example but it's  very useful if you do because you can  just do more stuff you can work on more  assignments whenever we would be looking  at candidates for traineeships we would  really also look at there at the  languages that they had and indeed I  mean we asked you owner to come and work  with us so for us French is not an  absolute requirement but it is really  good if you have it because in the  council a lot of French is still spoken  I feel but let's say that you don't have  French but you have another super useful  language may be Greek or maybe Finnish  or another language that can also be a  real asset  you see lots of applications from well  candidates with a background in EU  policy low international relations but  we also need trainees in information and  technology logistics meetings all these  kind of fields which are needed to run  the council during the application you  have to select your first preference and  second preference and there is a quite a  long list of preferences domains  available and these domains mirror the  activity of the council tivity in the  policy field but also in the  administration communication translation  professional experience is not not  required so it can also apply without  any professional experience if you have  the bachelor bachelor degree and it's  what you indicate as your domain first  domain and second domain is really up to  you up to your interest up to your  motivation so it can perfectly happen  that your studies are different what you  are interested in now but of course your  applications should be consistent so you  should have a deep knowledge of the view  of the domain what you are choosing for  I would really look at motivation and  try to see okay have these people done  their research have say you know checked  our website do they know roughly what  we're doing and is their motivation  quite strong I mean if it's just a  generic motivation saying oh this looks  interesting to me that's maybe not so  convincing but if people have clear  points even though they might lack the  experience in the field I can still be  be persuaded to pick somebody just  because you know it's not really fair to  ask of a ton of experience from people  who are just starting their career so I  totally get that I'd find that thing  that makes you unique find that thing in  your studies or your life in general and  your work experience that makes you  stand out and highlight that because  then there are a lot of applicants make  yourselves you know special  [Music]  we need a lot of extra hands on that we  need a lot of help watching social media  tracking you know seeing what what  journalists are saying about us trying  to sort of anticipate the news cycle and  trainees have played a super valuable  role in this regard because they've  really been our eyes and ears and they  help us to keep track of the huge volume  of communication that's happening about  the summit and then we're able to based  on all of the work they do were able to  in yeah inform our political principles  much better so that's also something  that I think trainees need to realize is  that our aim is not just to have you you  know there in the office and just look  on from the sidelines but really you're  gonna be doing a real job there are  tough days you you work hard you work  long hours but it's also very very  rewarding because you you get to be  really close to what is what is  happening that day what is decided that  they what is talked about that day  monitoring the media monitoring Twitter  social media and this is true you get to  get quite close to the leaders I would  usually come in at 9 o'clock depending  on the day sometimes if there's a summit  or a preparations for a summit then you  then you come in earlier but it's  usually an eight-hour workday but that  Secretariat that also varies a lot  because as I said if their summits if  there's something very important days  might drag on and that's that's normal  it really depends some days were a  little bit slower then I had more time  to do research and to teach myself new  things and then other days it was really  full-on press conferences running from A  to B to C to D and yeah but really as  Alexandra also mentioned earlier it is  it is full-on work  [Music]  a lot of it comes down to your the  accommodation that you're gonna get in  Brussels there's a number of options so  some places are expensive and some  places are less expensive where you're  gonna we're gonna live here but that  that is gonna take some chunk of the  money but there is gonna be money left  and and I think I lived you know in in a  nice manner with with the the money that  I received from the council I I had some  savings before I came here and I only  dipped into them just a little bit if I  get this it is sufficient enough amount  of money to have a social life to go to  the cinema to have a drink go to a  concert and yeah you can really live a  rich social life as well with the money  that you receive from the council  [Music]  usually we select 50 trainees so  applications and closes 16th of October  and then we start right away with the  selection procedure so the selection  will be ongoing in November December and  or aim is to contact selected trainees  before end of the year I mean that's the  aim sometimes happens that we are not  able to do that and we are still in  January and we are still contacting  potential potential trainees in January  but the aim is that to finish the  selection and have to select the  trainees by the end of the year if you  are selected or if you are on a  shortlist and invited for a phone  interview or on an interview then we  send you an email and if you are  selected you receive a traineeship offer  and through those trainee those  candidates who are not we're not  selected they will receive an email at  the end of the selection procedure  [Music]  during the years you see trainees who  have been at I mean they're coming back  in another professional capacity they  become delegates for a permanent  representations and processors they work  for NGO of King tanks or they come back  as working for the council quite a good  number of trainees stay on in browsers  and find find a job after they finish  appear we recently had a new colleague  join us in the web team and I had met  him the first time when he was on his  tail end of his traineeship and I had  just started in the press office it's  really fun to see people come back  because it I think it's a sign that this  the time they spent here was a good time  was a useful times I think the main  thing is that you need to be proactive  and you need to be open and you need to  be you really need to show the people  you work with that you're willing to  learn new things and that you yourself  have your own ideas that and you want to  contribute to the working environment  not just like I'm here to follow orders  obviously you need to know how to do  that as well but but really to push push  forward the fact that you are willing to  contribute something to the working  environment so be proactive that will be  my main tip a good trainee is definitely  somebody who is ready to work and to  work hard but who's also honest and open  when things don't really go as planned  when they struggle with something or  when they cannot meet a deadline or they  need some extra help because honestly  although we're trying to give you an  authentic work experience we also want  you to learn we want you to be able to  grow and benefit from this experience  [Music]  I would just say that apply and come  here because it's law it's a lot of fun  it's really you learn a lot and you  improve as an as an employee and  something that I have noticed applying  for jobs after afterwards there's a lot  more callbacks after used on the  traineeship so it really hit really pays  off to as you said in the beginning  leave your life and move to Brussels so  it's I do not regret that at all  [Music]

